     Question
In a bid to automate backup processes, the xFusionCorp Industries sysadmin team has developed a new bash script named xfusioncorp.sh. While the script has been distributed to all necessary servers, it lacks executable permissions on App Server 1 within the Stratos Datacenter.
Your task is to grant executable permissions to the /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh script on App Server 1. Additionally, ensure that all users have the capability to execute it.

    Solution
1. Login into App server1
    ssh tony@stapp01
2.Check current permissions
    ls -l /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
 You’ll likely see:
  -rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1234 May 20 19:45 /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
3-Add execute permission for all users
    sudo chmod a+x /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
    sudo chmod 755 /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
4-Check current permissios
    ls -l /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
 You'll likely see:
  -rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 1234 May 20 19:50 /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh

